---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';

const toc = [
  ['signals', 'What signals are read'],
  ['where', 'Where they live'],
  ['never-collected', 'What is never collected'],
  ['never-adapts', 'What never adapts'],
  ['dnt', 'Do Not Track and GPC'],
  ['pause', 'How to pause or reset'],
  ['contact', 'Contact'],
];
---

<Base
  title="Privacy: what Shapewell sees, and what it never does"
  description="Which behaviour signals Shapewell reads, where they live, what is never collected, what never adapts, and how Do Not Track and GPC are respected.">
  <section class="section privacy" aria-labelledby="pv-title">
    <div class="container grid-12 pv-grid">
      <header class="pv-head" data-slide="left">
        <SectionHead name="Privacy" />
        <h1 id="pv-title" class="h-display">What Shapewell sees, <span class="accent">and what it never does.</span></h1>
        <p class="label label-sm"><span class="c">Last updated</span> / 15 October 2026</p>
      </header>

      <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page" data-slide="left">
        <p class="label label-sm"><span class="c">On this page</span></p>
        <ol>
          {toc.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <article class="pv-body">
        <section id="signals" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">What signals are read</h2>
          <p>While you read a page that uses Shapewell, the script reads a few behaviour signals in your browser:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>How fast you scroll, as a rolling average in pixels per second, and how far down you got.</li>
            <li>How long certain sections were in view, and how long you rested the pointer on them (only counted after 1.2 seconds).</li>
            <li>Clicks on those sections, and whether you used the monthly or yearly billing toggle.</li>
            <li>Whether your device uses touch or a mouse.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>These are numbers about reading, not about you. You can watch every one of them live in the studio.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="where" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">Where they live</h2>
          <p>
            In memory, in the tab you have open. They are not written to cookies or storage, and they are not sent to a
            server. When you close the tab, they are gone.
          </p>
          <p>
            The one exception is a run or variant you choose to save with "Save this run" or "Save variant". That is stored
            in your browser's localStorage under <code>shapewell_runs</code>, on this device only, until you delete it from
            your library.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="never-collected" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">What is never collected</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Names, email addresses or account details.</li>
            <li>IP-based location.</li>
            <li>Device fingerprints or cross-site identifiers.</li>
            <li>Any personal data. The early access form on this demo does not send your email anywhere.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="never-adapts" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">What never adapts</h2>
          <p>
            Prices, checkout, and legal pages, including these terms. They are the same for everyone. Shapewell can reorder
            and shorten content, but it never hides information: every collapsed paragraph keeps a "Read more" button.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="dnt" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">Do Not Track and GPC</h2>
          <p>
            If your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, adapting is paused by default and the studio says
            so. You can still turn it on yourself, or replay a profile to see what would change.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="pause" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">How to pause or reset</h2>
          <p>
            Open the studio with the "Open studio" button or the K key. Use "Pause adapting" to stop changes, or "Reset to
            default" to clear the signals and return the page to its default shape.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="contact" data-slide="up">
          <h2 class="h-card">Contact</h2>
          <p>Questions about privacy: <a class="link" href="mailto:privacy@shapewell.dev">privacy@shapewell.dev</a>.</p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .pv-grid {
    align-items: start;
    row-gap: 32px;
  }
  .pv-head {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .pv-head .section-head {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .pv-head h1 {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .toc {
    grid-column: 1 / span 3;
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 24px);
  }
  .toc ol {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .toc a {
    display: block;
    padding: 10px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .toc a:hover {
    color: var(--cobalt);
  }
  .pv-body {
    grid-column: 5 / span 8;
  }
  .pv-body section {
    padding: 28px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .pv-body h2 {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .pv-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 1em;
    padding-left: 20px;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .pv-body li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--f-mono);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .toc,
    .pv-body {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
    .toc {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
